/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-032/src/kafka/docs/streams/developer-guide/interactive-queries.md:403:  * **Read-your-writes applies only to the single-key query.** Only `TimestampedKeyWithHeadersQuery` reads through the record cache, so it sees a write that has not yet been flushed to the store — unless you call `skipCache()`, or the entry has already been flushed. The range, window, and session queries bypass the cache entirely, so a not-yet-flushed write is invisible to them and, with a position bound, fails with a not-up-to-bound error.
